{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-104952",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To express the desired set, we start with the first integer divisible by $5$ greater than or equal to $-21,$ which is $-20.$ The next integer divisible by $5$ is $-15,$ the one after that is $-10,$ and so on up to $10$ (which is the last number that is divisible by $5$ and less than or equal to $11$).\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\{-20,-15,-10,…,10\\}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
